S:Norberto Romualdez et al., The Philippine Progressive Music Series for the Primary Grades, Silver Burdett, digitized volume revised through 1948, p. 25, "I Plant Some Rice," notation by Florencio Buado; HathiTrust Public Domain
N:CONTEXT: The page calls this an "Action Song" popular among Ilocano people. It assigns planting gestures to the first beats of printed measures 2, 3, 7 and 8; the later verses substitute harvesting, pounding, cooking and eating. Those claims document the schoolbook's instructions, not a present-day practice, and need Ilocano review.
N:HOW READ (2026-11-11): Printed p. 25 (PDF scan p. 34) was extracted at its embedded 600 ppi and checked as a complete page and enlarged score crops. The source counts the pickup as measure 1: m1 D4 eighth pickup; m2 G4-B4-D5-D4 eighths; m3 G4-B4-D5-B4 eighths; m4 D5 and C5 quarters; m5 A-sharp4 and B4 quarters; m6 G4 dotted quarter, D4 eighth; m7 repeats m2; m8 repeats m3; m9 D5 and B4 quarters; m10 A4 and G4 quarters; m11 F-sharp4 dotted quarter. The one-eighth pickup and three-eighth close balance, and every intervening bar totals four eighths. The source's action points at measures 2, 3, 7 and 8 independently corroborate this bar reading.
N:UNCERTAIN: The page prints no tempo, dynamics, accompaniment, source-language words, translation credit, collector, singer, collection date or place more specific than Ilocos Sur. It does not say whether the English text translates an Ilocano text or was newly fitted for school. HathiTrust's item-level Public Domain notice includes a general caveat about separately authored portions. A second plate reading and all named historical, language, cultural and classroom reviews remain required.
